What are the Types of modules in Node? 
===================================
In Node.js, there are three types of modules.

1) Built-in Modules (Core Modules)
-----------------------------------
Built-in modules are already available in Node.js.
We do not need to install them.
They give basic features.
Examples:
fs for file handling,
http for creating server,
path for file path.

2) Local Modules
------------------------
Local modules are created by us.
These are our own JavaScript files.
We use them to separate code and reuse code.

3) Third-Party Modules
---------------------------------
These modules are created by others and installed using npm
Third-party modules are created by other developers.
They are not available by default.
We install them using npm.
Example:
express, lodash

